Command:        ELO
Purpose:        Edit your login preferences
Available at:   All command prompts (>)

The ELO command will allow you to customize somewhat what modules are run during each time you login to the system.  Following are descriptions of the available options:

Test This Login         Choosing this option will do a "trial run" through
                        your selected options, as if you were first logging
                        in.  Remember that some options may not display
                        any output unless certain conditions are met.  (New
                        games started, new winners, etc.)

Reset to System Defaults
                        This option will reset your customized login sequence
                        to the default sequence defined by the sysop for your
                        terminal type.

Other options           The other options in this menu are sysop-defined
                        modules.  Each option should display a description of
                        what the option controls when it is selected.
